  "Question": "Which of the following is a quadratic equation in one variable?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x^2+2x=x^2-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2+1/x=2\\)",
    "C": "\\(x^2+y=1\\)",
    "D": "\\(3x^2-2x=1\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "In A, canceling \\(x^2\\) from both sides leaves a linear equation in one variable. B contains the fraction \\(1/x\\), so it is not a polynomial equation. C contains two unknowns. D can be rearranged as \\(3x^2-2x-1=0\\), which is a quadratic equation in one variable.",
